---
description: Conventions for hook scripts in this repository
globs: "**/hooks/*.mjs"
alwaysApply: false
---

This is the **Cursor rule** example: `globs` attaches it when matching files are in context; `alwaysApply: true` would attach it to every request.

- Hook scripts read one JSON payload from stdin and never prompt for input.
- Block only by exiting with code 2 and a reason on stderr; every supported tool honors that.
- Exit 0 on anything unexpected, so a bug in a hook never stops the agent.
- Don't log prompt or command text.
